-- ccc23-appeals.l4 -- sections 672.72 to 672.78 (Appeals) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46; 672.79 and 672.8 are repealed.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Form: see the header of ccc23-assessment.l4. The core `Party` has no constructor for the appellant: the regulative rule of 672.72(2) uses `the accused` (the party who most often appeals); NEEDS-CORE.md records "an appellant".

§ `Section 672.72 -- Grounds for appeal; limitation period`

-- 672.72(1): any party may appeal against a disposition made by a court or a Review Board, or a placement decision made by a Review Board, to the court of appeal of the province where the disposition or placement decision was made,
-- on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or fact alone or of mixed law and fact.
-- src:13854 | 672.72 (1) Any party may appeal against a disposition made by a court or a Review Board, or a placement decision made by a Review Board, to the court of appeal of the province where the disposition or placement decision was made on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or fact alone or of mixed law and fact.
@ref s 672.72(1) (src:13854)
GIVEN `the person is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a disposition made by a court or a Review Board, or a placement decision made by a Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is to the court of appeal of the province where the disposition or placement decision was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground raises a question of law or fact alone or of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.72(1) the party may appeal against the disposition or placement decision` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party` AND `it is a disposition made by a court or a Review Board, or a placement decision made by a Review Board` AND `the appeal is to the court of appeal of the province where the disposition or placement decision was made` AND `the ground raises a question of law or fact alone or of mixed law and fact`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any party may appeal against a disposition made by a court or a Review Board, or a placement decision made by a Review Board, to the court of appeal of the province where the disposition or placement decision was made"

-- 672.72(2): an appellant shall give notice of an appeal against a disposition or placement decision in the manner directed by the applicable rules of court within fifteen days after the day on which the appellant receives a copy of the placement decision or disposition and the reasons for it,
-- or within any further time that the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, may direct. As a regulative rule: the appellant's duty, within fifteen days.
-- src:13856 | (2) An appellant shall give notice of an appeal against a disposition or placement decision in the manner directed by the applicable rules of court within fifteen days after the day on which the appellant receives a copy of the placement decision or disposition and the reasons for it or within any further time that the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, may direct.
@ref s 672.72(2) (src:13856)
DECLARE `s 672.72(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.72(2) give notice of appeal`

@ref s 672.72(2) (src:13856)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 672.72(2) act`
`s 672.72(2) the appellant must give notice of appeal within fifteen days` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 672.72(2) give notice of appeal`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "notice of appeal was not given within fifteen days after the appellant received a copy of the disposition or placement decision and the reasons for it"

-- The same duty as a decision function over dates: the fifteen days run from the day after the appellant receives the copy and the reasons (the text says "within fifteen days after the day on which"); a further time directed by the court of appeal or a judge replaces them.
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
@ref s 672.72(2) (src:13856)
GIVEN `the day the appellant receives a copy of the disposition or placement decision and the reasons for it` IS A DATE
      `the day the appellant gives notice of appeal` IS A DATE
      `the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, has directed a further time, to the end of` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.72(2) notice of appeal is given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the appellant gives notice of appeal` AT MOST (`the day the appellant receives a copy of the disposition or placement decision and the reasons for it` PLUS 15)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, has directed a further time, to the end of`
         WHEN JUST further THEN (IF `the day the appellant gives notice of appeal` AT MOST further THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within fifteen days after the day on which the appellant receives a copy of the placement decision or disposition and the reasons for it or within any further time that the court of appeal, or a judge of that court, may direct"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within fifteen days after the day on which the appellant receives a copy of the placement decision or disposition and the reasons for it"

-- 672.72(3): the court of appeal shall hear an appeal against a disposition or placement decision in or out of the regular sessions of the court, as soon as practicable after the day on which the notice of appeal is given, within any period that may be fixed by the court of appeal,
-- a judge of the court of appeal, or the rules of that court. The period is fixed by the court or its rules, outside the sources: it is an input, and where none is fixed the text sets no number (NOTHING).
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
-- src:13858 | (3) The court of appeal shall hear an appeal against a disposition or placement decision in or out of the regular sessions of the court, as soon as practicable after the day on which the notice of appeal is given, within any period that may be fixed by the court of appeal, a judge of the court of appeal, or the rules of that court.
@ref s 672.72(3) (src:13858)
GIVEN `the day notice of appeal is given` IS A DATE
      `the period fixed by the court of appeal, a judge of that court, or the rules of that court, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the day the court of appeal hears the appeal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.72(3) the court of appeal hears the appeal within the period fixed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period fixed by the court of appeal, a judge of that court, or the rules of that court, in days`
    WHEN JUST days THEN (IF `the day the court of appeal hears the appeal` AT MOST (`the day notice of appeal is given` PLUS days) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within any period that may be fixed by the court of appeal, a judge of the court of appeal, or the rules of that court"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "within any period that may be fixed by the court of appeal, a judge of the court of appeal, or the rules of that court"

§ `Sections 672.73 to 672.75 -- The appeal`

-- 672.73(1): an appeal against a disposition by a court or Review Board or placement decision by a Review Board shall be based on a transcript of the proceedings and any other evidence that the court of appeal finds necessary to admit in the interests of justice.
-- src:13860 | 672.73 (1) An appeal against a disposition by a court or Review Board or placement decision by a Review Board shall be based on a transcript of the proceedings and any other evidence that the court of appeal finds necessary to admit in the interests of justice.
@ref s 672.73(1) (src:13860)
GIVEN `it is an appeal against a disposition by a court or Review Board or a placement decision by a Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.73(1) the appeal is based on a transcript of the proceedings and any other evidence that the court of appeal finds necessary to admit` MEANS
    IF `it is an appeal against a disposition by a court or Review Board or a placement decision by a Review Board`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal against a disposition by a court or Review Board or placement decision by a Review Board"

-- 672.73(2): for the purpose of admitting additional evidence under this section, subsections 683(1) and (2) apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require.
-- src:13862 | (2) For the purpose of admitting additional evidence under this section, subsections 683(1) and (2) apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require.
