§ `Sections 672.76 to 672.78 -- Pending the appeal; powers of the court of appeal`

-- 672.76(1): any party who gives notice to each of the other parties, within the time and in the manner prescribed, may apply to a judge of the court of appeal for an order under this section respecting a disposition or placement decision that is under appeal.
-- src:13879 | 672.76 (1) Any party who gives notice to each of the other parties, within the time and in the manner prescribed, may apply to a judge of the court of appeal for an order under this section respecting a disposition or placement decision that is under appeal.
@ref s 672.76(1) (src:13879)
GIVEN `the person is a party who gives notice to each of the other parties, within the time and in the manner prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disposition or placement decision is under appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.76(1) the party may apply to a judge of the court of appeal for an order respecting the decision under appeal` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party who gives notice to each of the other parties, within the time and in the manner prescribed` AND `the disposition or placement decision is under appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any party who gives notice to each of the other parties, within the time and in the manner prescribed"

-- 672.76(2): on receipt of an application, a judge of the court of appeal may, if satisfied that the mental condition of the accused justifies it, (a) direct that a disposition made under section 672.58 be carried out pending the determination of the appeal, despite section 672.75;
-- (a.1) direct that a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(a) be suspended pending the determination of the appeal; (b) direct that the application of a placement decision or a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(b) or (c) be suspended pending the determination of the appeal;
-- (c) where the application of a disposition is suspended pursuant to section 672.75 or paragraph (b), make any other disposition in respect of the accused that is appropriate in the circumstances, other than a disposition under paragraph 672.54(a) or section 672.58, pending the determination of the appeal;
-- (d) where the application of a placement decision is suspended pursuant to an order made under paragraph (b), make any other placement decision that is appropriate in the circumstances, pending the determination of the appeal; and (e) give any directions that the judge considers necessary for expediting the appeal.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF, F-GRANT-WHERE
