-- src:13895 | (b) it is based on a wrong decision on a question of law; or
-- src:13896 | (c) there was a miscarriage of justice.
@ref s 672.78(1); s 672.78(1)(a); s 672.78(1)(b); s 672.78(1)(c) (src:13893-13896)
GIVEN `the court of appeal is of the opinion that the disposition or placement decision is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the court of appeal is of the opinion that it is based on a wrong decision on a question of law` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the court of appeal is of the opinion that there was a miscarriage of justice` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.78(1) the court of appeal may allow the appeal and set aside the order` MEANS
    IF `the court of appeal is of the opinion that the disposition or placement decision is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence` OR `the court of appeal is of the opinion that it is based on a wrong decision on a question of law` OR `the court of appeal is of the opinion that there was a miscarriage of justice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the court of appeal is of the opinion that"

-- 672.78(2): the court of appeal may dismiss an appeal against a disposition or placement decision where the court is of the opinion (a) that paragraphs (1)(a), (b) and (c) do not apply; or (b) that paragraph (1)(b) may apply, but the court finds that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13898 | (2) The court of appeal may dismiss an appeal against a disposition or placement decision where the court is of the opinion
-- src:13899 | (a) that paragraphs (1)(a), (b) and (c) do not apply; or
-- src:13900 | (b) that paragraph (1)(b) may apply, but the court finds that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred.
@ref s 672.78(2); s 672.78(2)(a); s 672.78(2)(b) (src:13898-13900)
GIVEN `the court is of the opinion that paragraphs 672.78(1)(a), (b) and (c) do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the court is of the opinion that paragraph 672.78(1)(b) may apply` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the court finds that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.78(2) the court of appeal may dismiss the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the court is of the opinion that paragraphs 672.78(1)(a), (b) and (c) do not apply` OR (`the court is of the opinion that paragraph 672.78(1)(b) may apply` AND `the court finds that no substantial wrong or miscarriage of justice has occurred`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the court is of the opinion"

-- 672.78(3): where the court of appeal allows an appeal against a disposition or placement decision, it may (a) make any disposition under section 672.54 or any placement decision that the Review Board could have made;
-- (b) refer the matter back to the court or Review Board for re-hearing, in whole or in part, in accordance with any directions that the court of appeal considers appropriate; or (c) make any other order that justice requires.
-- fork: F-GRANT-WHERE
-- src:13902 | (3) Where the court of appeal allows an appeal against a disposition or placement decision, it may
-- src:13903 | (a) make any disposition under section 672.54 or any placement decision that the Review Board could have made;
-- src:13904 | (b) refer the matter back to the court or Review Board for re-hearing, in whole or in part, in accordance with any directions that the court of appeal considers appropriate; or
-- src:13905 | (c) make any other order that justice requires.
@ref s 672.78(3); s 672.78(3)(a); s 672.78(3)(b); s 672.78(3)(c) (src:13902-13905)
GIVEN `the court of appeal allows an appeal against a disposition or placement decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.78(3) the court of appeal may make a disposition or placement decision the Review Board could have made, refer the matter back, or make any other order that justice requires` MEANS
    IF `the court of appeal allows an appeal against a disposition or placement decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court of appeal allows an appeal against a disposition or placement decision"

